# Build with:  latexmk -pdf -jobname=_v -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex
# If a PDF viewer holds the output open, pdflatex cannot write it and the build
# dies with "I can't write on file". Build to another jobname instead.

# LaTeX build artifacts, all regenerated.
*.aux
*.log
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.out
*.run.xml
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*-SAVE-ERROR

# Every PDF is a build product EXCEPT the one committed copy and the figures.
# Stated as an allowlist so no new jobname or draft can leak into the history.
*.pdf
!thesis_v2.pdf
!figs/*.pdf

# Harnesses, per-figure compile scaffolding, superseded drafts and the design-phase
# specimens. Kept on disk because several figures are compiled in isolation through
# them, but they are working files and do not belong in the history.
_scratch/
_*.tex
_*.py
